<article class="env-lemma" id="07ZU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07ZU">Lemma <span data-tag="07ZU">31.14.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $D \subset S$ be an effective Cartier divisor. Let $U = S \setminus D$. Then $U \to S$ is an affine morphism and $U$ is scheme theoretically dense in $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Affineness is Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZT" data-tag="07ZT">31.14.3</a>. The density question is local on $S$, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01RE" data-tag="01RE">29.7.5</a>. Thus we may assume $S = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ and $D$ corresponding to the nonzerodivisor $f \in A$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/01WS" data-tag="01WS">31.14.2</a>. Thus $A \subset A_ f$ which implies that $U \subset S$ is scheme theoretically dense, see Morphisms, Example <a href="/tag/056C" data-tag="056C">29.7.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>